      "risk": "Same path-parameter type risk: 'a1' is a valid account ID but not an int.",
      "observable": "POST /accounts/a1/withdraw currently processes the request; with account_id: int it would return 422 before any business logic."
    },
    {
      "route": "POST /accounts/<account_id>/withdraw",
      "risk": "Account lookup occurs before request body validation in Flask. FastAPI validates the body before calling the handler, so a missing account with a bad body can produce a different error.",
      "observable": "POST /accounts/nonexistent/withdraw with an empty body currently returns 404 {\"error\":\"not_found\",\"resource\":\"account\"}; FastAPI typed body handling would return 422 field-required validation detail."
    },
    {
      "route": "POST /accounts/<account_id>/withdraw",
      "risk": "request.get_json(silent=True) or {} treats missing, empty, or invalid JSON as an empty dict. A typed Pydantic body rejects these instead.",
      "observable": "Empty or invalid JSON to an existing account currently returns 400 {\"error\":\"bad_amount\"}; FastAPI would return 422 with validation detail."
    },
    {
      "route": "POST /accounts/<account_id>/withdraw",
      "risk": "Legacy amount validation requires isinstance(amount, int); Pydantic int fields coerce JSON strings like \"5\" into integers.",
      "observable": "Body {\"amount\":\"5\"} currently returns 400 {\"error\":\"bad_amount\"}; with amount: int it would succeed and return 200 with withdrawn 5."
    },
    {
      "route": "POST /accounts/<account_id>/withdraw",
      "risk": "Non-positive or missing amount returns the custom 400 bad_amount payload. FastAPI validation with gt=0 (or required fields) uses the 422 validation envelope.",
      "observable": "Amount 0, -1, or missing changes from 400 {\"error\":\"bad_amount\"} to 422 {\"detail\":[...]}."
    },
    {
      "route": "POST /accounts/<account_id>/withdraw",
      "risk": "InsufficientFunds relies on a custom exception handler that returns 409 with needed and available. Raising HTTPException or leaving the exception unhandled loses that contract.",
