  "notes": "Existing clients parse a uniform error envelope with an \"error\" key and, for HTTP errors, \"status\" and \"message\". The special 409 payload must keep \"needed\" and \"available\". The route handlers also return exact success keys: account objects have id/balance; withdraw responses have id/withdrawn/balance. Any migration that switches to FastAPI's default validation or exception payloads will break these clients, even if the numeric status code is preserved."
